  "correctedAt": "2026-11-06 (Section 187.1), 2026-11-13 (Section 194), 2026-11-13 (Section 194.7)",
  "correction": "Section 187.1: verifyReachability could not see a call written with optional chaining on every link (`rama?.ns?.member?.()`), so 16 members with real renderer callers were listed here as orphans. The register was OVERSTATING the debt. The matcher now normalises `?.` and these 16 are removed. This list may still only shrink. CORRECTED AGAIN in Section 194: the matcher's loose rule required an ASSIGNMENT (= window.rama.<ns>), so a namespace reached through a service wrapper that RETURNS it (const ipc = () => window.rama?.auth) read as unreached. All twenty auth members were false orphans though the app cannot log anyone in without them. 78 entries removed, leaving 203. CORRECTED A THIRD TIME in Section 194.7: the service layer in src/services/ipcClient.js dispatches by STRING - ipc('system.getProcesses', user) walks the path on window.rama - so no window.rama.<ns>.<name> chain exists for eight namespaces and every member reached that way counted only through the loose rule, or not at all. Matching the quoted member path closes the computed-property blind spot this suite had declared held by hand since Section 143. 25 entries removed, leaving 178.",
