  "unsurfacedChannelsWhy": "Baseline for verifyReachability.cjs rule 4 (spec Section 195). Each entry is a channel registered in the main process that NO renderer file names and whose bridge members all have no caller - capability with no reader, as opposed to rule 3's register which also counts members whose channel is reached by another route. THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. CORRECTED ON THE DAY IT WAS SEEDED: the first run of this rule enumerated ipcRenderer method names and so missed sendSync('window:is-maximized'), and it counted preload plumbing - app:preload-error, sent when contextBridge refuses a value, and badge:clicked, sent from the badge window's own preload - as capability with no reader. Neither can be reached by a page and neither should be. 3 removed, leaving 137."
